logs/

# ...but NOT the public benchmark publication contract's logs. The bare `logs/`
# above is a Pulse-runtime rule; it also matches
# `reports/benchmarks/publication/<run>/logs/`, where
# scripts/run_public_benchmarks.sh writes the three `*.stderr.log` artifacts
# that REQUIRED_RUN_ARTIFACTS demands. The 2026-08-10-pristine run recorded all
# three in current.json with their sha256 and byte counts and committed none of
# them, because git silently refused: the checker has read
# "missing required artifact" ever since, for a reason no amount of re-running
# the suite would have fixed. Both lines are needed -- git will not re-include a
# file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so the directory must be un-excluded
# first.
!reports/benchmarks/publication/**/logs/
!reports/benchmarks/publication/**/logs/**

# Benchmark outputs
benchmarks/**/results/
benchmarks/**/logs/
benchmarks/**/data/

