/publish/.out/

# Isabelle/HOL KernelVerified shards (released as archives, not git-tracked)
data/mathverse-shards/isabelle-hol-kv/

# nat-operand-shape probe runner output. The pinned expectations are the
# `--@ probe-expect:` headers in probes/*.lean, which ARE tracked; this file is
# a convenience table whose `ms` fields change on every run. Tracking it would
# make a routine gate run dirty the tree -- the trap CLAUDE.md documents for
# data/suite_state/, where one `git checkout` over runner output destroyed a
# 14-hour sweep with exit 0.
tests/nat-operand-shape-probe/matrix.json
.metadata_never_index

# Compiler crash dumps. rustc and the Trust tools write `<tool>-ice-<time>.txt`
# into the directory they were invoked from, which for this repo is almost
# always the root; nine of them were once committed under reports/ice/ and
# outlived the defects they recorded. Anchored to the ROOT only, so a dump that
# is deliberately filed elsewhere (e.g. under reports/) can still be committed.
/rustc-ice-*.txt
/trustc-ice-*.txt
/trustfmt-ice-*.txt
/trustdoc-ice-*.txt
